{"id":"mahabharata-9-057","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":57,"title":"सप्तपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 57 · Krishna's counsel to Arjuna","summary":{"en":"As the fight grows, Krishna tells Arjuna that Bhima cannot overcome Duryodhana in fair fight and must remember his vow to break Duryodhana's thigh. Arjuna strikes his own left thigh as a signal to Bhima, and Bhima understands.","kn":"ಯುದ್ಧ ತೀವ್ರವಾದಂತೆ ನ್ಯಾಯಯುದ್ಧದಲ್ಲಿ ಭೀಮ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನನ್ನು ಗೆಲ್ಲಲಾರನೆಂದು, ತೊಡೆ ಮುರಿಯುವ ಪ್ರತಿಜ್ಞೆ ನೆನಪಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನ ತನ್ನ ಎಡತೊಡೆಗೆ ಹೊಡೆದು ಭೀಮನಿಗೆ ಸಂಕೇತ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮ ಅರ್ಥಮಾಡಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"युद्ध तीव्र होने पर कृष्ण अर्जुन से कहते हैं कि भीम न्यायपूर्ण लड़ाई में दुर्योधन को नहीं जीत सकते और उन्हें जंघा तोड़ने की प्रतिज्ञा याद करनी होगी। अर्जुन अपनी बाईं जंघा पर थपकी देकर भीम को संकेत देते हैं और भीम समझ जाते हैं।","te":"యుద్ధం తీవ్రమవగా న్యాయ పోరులో భీముడు దుర్యోధనుని గెలవలేడని, తొడ విరిచే ప్రతిజ్ఞను గుర్తు చేయాలని కృష్ణుడు అర్జునునికి చెబుతాడు. అర్జునుడు తన ఎడమ తొడను కొట్టి భీమునికి సంకేతమివ్వగా భీముడు గ్రహిస్తాడు.","ta":"போர் தீவிரமாக, நியாயப் போரில் பீமன் துரியோதனனை வெல்ல முடியாது, தொடையை முறிக்கும் சபதத்தை நினைவுகொள்ள வேண்டும் என்று கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனிடம் கூறுகிறார். அர்ஜுனன் தன் இடத் தொடையைத் தட்டிப் பீமனுக்குக் குறிப்புக் காட்ட, பீமன் புரிந்துகொள்கிறான்.","ml":"പോരാട്ടം മുറുകുമ്പോൾ, ന്യായമായ യുദ്ധത്തിൽ ദുര്യോധനനെ ഭീമന് കീഴടക്കാനാവില്ലെന്ന് കൃഷ്ണൻ അർജുനനോട് പറയുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനന്റെ തുട തകർക്കുമെന്ന പ്രതിജ്ഞ ഭീമൻ ഓർക്കണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. ഭീമന് സൂചന നൽകാൻ അർജുനൻ തന്റെ ഇടത്തെ തുടയിൽ അടിക്കുന്നു; ഭീമൻ കാര്യം മനസ്സിലാക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.57; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"गदायुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Gadayuddha Parva (The mace fight)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"समुदीर्णं ततो दृष्ट्वा संग्रामं कुरुमुख्ययोः ।\nअथाब्रवीदर्जुनस्तु वासुदेवं यशस्विनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the battle between the two foremost Kurus rise to its height, Arjuna spoke to the renowned Vasudeva."}},{"n":2,"text":"अनयोर्वीरयोर्युद्धे को ज्यायान्भवतो मतः ।\nकस्य वा को गुणो भूयानेतद्वद जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who, in your view, is the greater of these two heroes in this fight, Janardana? Which of them has more of what qualities? Tell me this.\""}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"उपदेशोऽनयोस्तुल्यो भीमस्तु बलवत्तरः ।\nकृतयत्नतरस्त्वेष धार्तराष्ट्रो वृकोदरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their training was equal, but Bhima is the stronger; Dhritarashtra's son, however, has worked harder at it than Vrikodara."}},{"n":4,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु धर्मेण युध्यमानो न जेष्यति ।\nअन्यायेन तु युध्यन्वै हन्यादेष सुयोधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, fighting by dharma, will not win; but fighting unfairly he could kill Suyodhana."}},{"n":5,"text":"मायया निर्जिता देवैरसुरा इति नः श्रुतम् ।\nविरोचनश्च शक्रेण मायया निर्जितः सखे ।\nमायया चाक्षिपत्तेजो वृत्रस्य बलसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard that the asuras were beaten by the gods through trickery; Virochana too was beaten by Indra through trickery, friend; and the slayer of Bala by trickery drew out Vritra's power."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रतिज्ञातं तु भीमेन द्यूतकाले धनंजय ।\nऊरू भेत्स्यामि ते संख्ये गदयेति सुयोधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima made a vow at the time of the dice game, Dhananjaya: \"I shall break your thighs in battle with my mace,\" he said to Suyodhana."}},{"n":7,"text":"सोऽयं प्रतिज्ञां तां चापि पारयित्वारिकर्शनः ।\nमायाविनं च राजानं माययैव निकृन्ततु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let this tormentor of his foes fulfil that vow and cut down by trickery the tricky king."}},{"n":8,"text":"यद्येष बलमास्थाय न्यायेन प्रहरिष्यति ।\nविषमस्थस्ततो राजा भविष्यति युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If Bhima fights this king fairly, relying on strength, King Yudhishthira will be in a perilous position."}},{"n":9,"text":"पुनरेव च वक्ष्यामि पाण्डवेदं निबोध मे ।\nधर्मराजापराधेन भयं नः पुनरागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall say more, Pandava; listen to me. Through the fault of King Yudhishthira, danger has come to us again."}},{"n":10,"text":"कृत्वा हि सुमहत्कर्म हत्वा भीष्ममुखान्कुरून् ।\nजयः प्राप्तो यशश्चाग्र्यं वैरं च प्रतियातितम् ।\nतदेवं विजयः प्राप्तः पुनः संशयितः कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having done a very great deed, killing the Kurus led by Bhishma, we had won victory, the finest fame, and had repaid the enmity; yet victory once won has again been put in doubt."}},{"n":11,"text":"अबुद्धिरेषा महती धर्मराजस्य पाण्डव ।\nयदेकविजये युद्धं पणितं कृतमीदृशम् ।\nसुयोधनः कृती वीर एकायनगतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is a great lack of judgement in King Yudhishthira, Pandava, that he made such a wager for the battle, staking everything on a single victory, when Suyodhana is a skilled hero with a single refuge."}},{"n":12,"text":"अपि चोशनसा गीतः श्रूयतेऽयं पुरातनः ।\nश्लोकस्तत्त्वार्थसहितस्तन्मे निगदतः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"An old verse sung by Ushanas is also remembered, full of true meaning; hear it from me as I recite."}},{"n":13,"text":"पुनरावर्तमानानां भग्नानां जीवितैषिणाम् ।\nभेतव्यमरिशेषाणामेकायनगता हि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those who survive, broken and returning, wishing to live, are to be feared by their enemies, for they have a single refuge.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"सुयोधनमिमं भग्नं हतसैन्यं ह्रदं गतम् ।\nपराजितं वनप्रेप्सुं निराशं राज्यलम्भने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Here is this Suyodhana, broken, his army destroyed, gone into the lake, defeated, wishing to go to the forest and hopeless of regaining the kingdom.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"को न्वेष संयुगे प्राज्ञः पुनर्द्वंद्वे समाह्वयेत् ।\nअपि वो निर्जितं राज्यं न हरेत सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What wise man would challenge him again to single combat in battle? Would not Suyodhana take back from you even the kingdom you have won?\""}},{"n":16,"text":"यस्त्रयोदशवर्षाणि गदया कृतनिश्रमः ।\nचरत्यूर्ध्वं च तिर्यक्च भीमसेनजिघांसया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For thirteen years he has trained tirelessly with the mace, moving up and down and across, wishing to kill Bhimasena.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"एवं चेन्न महाबाहुरन्यायेन हनिष्यति ।\nएष वः कौरवो राजा धार्तराष्ट्रो भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If the mighty-armed Bhima does not kill him by unfair means, this Kaurava, Dhritarashtra's son, will be your king.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"धनंजयस्तु श्रुत्वैतत्केशवस्य महात्मनः ।\nप्रेक्षतो भीमसेनस्य हस्तेनोरुमताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words of the great-souled Keshava, Dhananjaya, as Bhimasena looked on, struck his own thigh with his hand."}},{"n":19,"text":"गृह्य संज्ञां ततो भीमो गदया व्यचरद्रणे ।\nमण्डलानि विचित्राणि यमकानीतराणि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the sign, Bhima moved through the battle with his mace, in varied circling movements, paired and otherwise,"}},{"n":20,"text":"दक्षिणं मण्डलं सव्यं गोमूत्रकमथापि च ।\nव्यचरत्पाण्डवो राजन्नरिं संमोहयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"right-hand circles, left-hand ones, and zigzag, O king, moving as though to bewilder the enemy."}},{"n":21,"text":"तथैव तव पुत्रोऽपि गदामार्गविशारदः ।\nव्यचरल्लघु चित्रं च भीमसेनजिघांसया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son likewise, expert in the paths of the mace, moved nimbly and in varied ways, wishing to kill Bhimasena."}},{"n":22,"text":"आधुन्वन्तौ गदे घोरे चन्दनागरुरूषिते ।\nवैरस्यान्तं परीप्सन्तौ रणे क्रुद्धाविवान्तकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both whirled their fearsome maces, smeared with sandal and aloe, seeking an end to the enmity, like two furious Deaths."}},{"n":23,"text":"अन्योन्यं तौ जिघांसन्तौ प्रवीरौ पुरुषर्षभौ ।\nयुयुधाते गरुत्मन्तौ यथा नागामिषैषिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eager to kill each other, those two heroes, bulls among men, fought like two Garudas hunting a snake for food."}},{"n":24,"text":"मण्डलानि विचित्राणि चरतोर्नृपभीमयोः ।\nगदासंपातजास्तत्र प्रजज्ञुः पावकार्चिषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the king and Bhima moved in their varied circles, flames sprang up there from the falling of the maces."}},{"n":25,"text":"समं प्रहरतोस्तत्र शूरयोर्बलिनोर्मृधे ।\nक्षुब्धयोर्वायुना राजन्द्वयोरिव समुद्रयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two strong heroes struck equally in the battle, like two oceans stirred by the wind, O king."}},{"n":26,"text":"तयोः प्रहरतोस्तुल्यं मत्तकुञ्जरयोरिव ।\nगदानिर्घातसंह्रादः प्रहाराणामजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they struck on equal terms like two rutting elephants, a thunderous roar of blows from the maces arose."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्मिंस्तदा संप्रहारे दारुणे संकुले भृशम् ।\nउभावपि परिश्रान्तौ युध्यमानावरिंदमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that fierce, crowded and violent exchange, both subduers of enemies grew weary as they fought."}},{"n":28,"text":"तौ मुहूर्तं समाश्वस्य पुनरेव परंतपौ ।\nअभ्यहारयतां क्रुद्धौ प्रगृह्य महती गदे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two scorchers of foes, after resting a moment, raised their great maces in anger and attacked again."}},{"n":29,"text":"तयोः समभवद्युद्धं घोररूपमसंवृतम् ।\nगदानिपातै राजेन्द्र तक्षतोर्वै परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A terrible, unrestrained battle arose between them, O king of kings, as they hacked at each other with falling maces."}},{"n":30,"text":"व्यायामप्रद्रुतौ तौ तु वृषभाक्षौ तरस्विनौ ।\nअन्योन्यं जघ्नतुर्वीरौ पङ्कस्थौ महिषाविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Driven by exertion, those two mighty, bull-eyed heroes struck each other like two buffaloes standing in mud."}},{"n":31,"text":"जर्जरीकृतसर्वाङ्गौ रुधिरेणाभिसंप्लुतौ ।\nददृशाते हिमवति पुष्पिताविव किंशुकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With their whole bodies cut up and drenched in blood, they looked like two flowering kimshuka trees on the Himalaya."}},{"n":32,"text":"दुर्योधनेन पार्थस्तु विवरे संप्रदर्शिते ।\nईषदुत्स्मयमानस्तु सहसा प्रससार ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Duryodhana showed an opening, the son of Pritha, smiling slightly, suddenly advanced."}},{"n":33,"text":"तमभ्याशगतं प्राज्ञो रणे प्रेक्ष्य वृकोदरः ।\nअवाक्षिपद्गदां तस्मै वेगेन महता बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him come close in the battle, the wise Vrikodara, powerful, hurled his mace at him with great speed."}},{"n":34,"text":"अवक्षेपं तु तं दृष्ट्वा पुत्रस्तव विशां पते ।\nअपासर्पत्ततः स्थानात्सा मोघा न्यपतद्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that throw, your son, O lord of men, slipped away from the spot, and the mace fell uselessly on the ground."}},{"n":35,"text":"मोक्षयित्वा प्रहारं तं सुतस्तव स संभ्रमात् ।\nभीमसेनं च गदया प्राहरत्कुरुसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having evaded that blow, your son in haste struck Bhimasena with his mace, that best of the Kurus."}},{"n":36,"text":"तस्य विष्यन्दमानेन रुधिरेणामितौजसः ।\nप्रहारगुरुपाताच्च मूर्छेव समजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the blood streaming from him, that one of boundless might, and from the heavy fall of the blow, a swoon seemed to come over him."}},{"n":37,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तं च वेद पीडितं पाण्डवं रणे ।\nधारयामास भीमोऽपि शरीरमतिपीडितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana knew that the Pandava was hurt in the battle; Bhima too held up his badly hurt body."}},{"n":38,"text":"अमन्यत स्थितं ह्येनं प्रहरिष्यन्तमाहवे ।\nअतो न प्राहरत्तस्मै पुनरेव तवात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana thought Bhima was standing ready to strike in the fight, and so your son did not strike at him again."}},{"n":39,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तमाश्वस्य दुर्योधनमवस्थितम् ।\nवेगेनाभ्यद्रवद्राजन्भीमसेनः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after resting a moment, mighty Bhimasena rushed with speed at Duryodhana, who stood there, O king."}},{"n":40,"text":"तमापतन्तं संप्रेक्ष्य संरब्धममितौजसम् ।\nमोघमस्य प्रहारं तं चिकीर्षुर्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him charging in fury, of boundless might, and wishing to make his blow miss, O best of Bharatas,"}},{"n":41,"text":"अवस्थाने मतिं कृत्वा पुत्रस्तव महामनाः ।\nइयेषोत्पतितुं राजंश्छलयिष्यन्वृकोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"your high-minded son, resolving to stand, wanted to leap up in order to cheat Vrikodara."}},{"n":42,"text":"अबुध्यद्भीमसेनस्तद्राज्ञस्तस्य चिकीर्षितम् ।\nअथास्य समभिद्रुत्य समुत्क्रम्य च सिंहवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena understood what the king meant to do; he rushed up and sprang past him like a lion."}},{"n":43,"text":"सृत्या वञ्चयतो राजन्पुनरेवोत्पतिष्यतः ।\nऊरुभ्यां प्राहिणोद्राजन्गदां वेगेन पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the king, evading by a quick movement, was about to leap up again, the Pandava sent his mace at his thighs with great speed."}},{"n":44,"text":"सा वज्रनिष्पेषसमा प्रहिता भीमकर्मणा ।\nऊरू दुर्योधनस्याथ बभञ्ज प्रियदर्शनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hurled by Bhima's terrible deed, it was like a thunderbolt crashing down, and it broke Duryodhana's fine thighs."}},{"n":45,"text":"स पपात नरव्याघ्रो वसुधामनुनादयन् ।\nभग्नोरुर्भीमसेनेन पुत्रस्तव महीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son, that tiger among men, fell, making the earth resound, his thighs broken by Bhimasena, O lord of the earth."}},{"n":46,"text":"ववुर्वाताः सनिर्घाताः पांसुवर्षं पपात च ।\nचचाल पृथिवी चापि सवृक्षक्षुपपर्वता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Winds blew with crashes, dust rained down, and the earth shook with its trees, shrubs and mountains."}},{"n":47,"text":"तस्मिन्निपतिते वीरे पत्यौ सर्वमहीक्षिताम् ।\nमहास्वना पुनर्दीप्ता सनिर्घाता भयंकरी ।\nपपात चोल्का महती पतिते पृथिवीपतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that hero, lord of all kings, fell, a great, loud, blazing, fearful meteor, with crashes, fell, as the lord of the earth fell."}},{"n":48,"text":"तथा शोणितवर्षं च पांसुवर्षं च भारत ।\nववर्ष मघवांस्तत्र तव पुत्रे निपातिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A rain of blood and a rain of dust, O Bharata, was sent down there by Indra when your son was struck down."}},{"n":49,"text":"यक्षाणां राक्षसानां च पिशाचानां तथैव च ।\nअन्तरिक्षे महानादः श्रूयते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great cry of yakshas, rakshasas and pishachas was heard in the sky, O best of Bharatas."}},{"n":50,"text":"तेन शब्देन घोरेण मृगाणामथ पक्षिणाम् ।\nजज्ञे घोरतमः शब्दो बहूनां सर्वतोदिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From that terrible sound, a still more terrible noise arose from many beasts and birds in all directions."}},{"n":51,"text":"ये तत्र वाजिनः शेषा गजाश्च मनुजैः सह ।\nमुमुचुस्ते महानादं तव पुत्रे निपातिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The horses that remained there, and the elephants and men, cried out loudly when your son was felled."}},{"n":52,"text":"भेरीशङ्खमृदङ्गानामभवच्च स्वनो महान् ।\nअन्तर्भूमिगतश्चैव तव पुत्रे निपातिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sound of drums, conches and mridangas was great, and it came from under the ground when your son was felled."}},{"n":53,"text":"बहुपादैर्बहुभुजैः कबन्धैर्घोरदर्शनैः ।\nनृत्यद्भिर्भयदैर्व्याप्ता दिशस्तत्राभवन्नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"The directions were filled there, O king, with fearful headless bodies of many feet and arms, dancing horribly."}},{"n":54,"text":"ध्वजवन्तोऽस्त्रवन्तश्च शस्त्रवन्तस्तथैव च ।\nप्राकम्पन्त ततो राजंस्तव पुत्रे निपातिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the banners, the missiles and the weapons shook, O king, when your son was felled."}},{"n":55,"text":"ह्रदाः कूपाश्च रुधिरमुद्वेमुर्नृपसत्तम ।\nनद्यश्च सुमहावेगाः प्रतिस्रोतोवहाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lakes and wells spewed blood, O best of kings, and mighty rivers flowed backwards."}},{"n":56,"text":"पुल्लिङ्गा इव नार्यस्तु स्त्रीलिङ्गाः पुरुषाभवन् ।\nदुर्योधने तदा राजन्पतिते तनये तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Women seemed like men and men like women, O king, when your son Duryodhana fell."}},{"n":57,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तानद्भुतोत्पातान्पाञ्चालाः पाण्डवैः सह ।\nआविग्नमनसः सर्वे बभूवुर्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those marvellous omens, the Panchalas with the Pandavas were all troubled in mind, O best of Bharatas."}},{"n":58,"text":"ययुर्देवा यथाकामं गन्धर्वाप्सरसस्तथा ।\nकथयन्तोऽद्भुतं युद्धं सुतयोस्तव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods, gandharvas and apsaras went away as they pleased, speaking of the wonderful battle between your two sons, O Bharata."}},{"n":59,"text":"तथैव सिद्धा राजेन्द्र तथा वातिकचारणाः ।\nनरसिंहौ प्रशंसन्तौ विप्रजग्मुर्यथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise the Siddhas, Vatikas and Charanas, O king of kings, went away as they had come, praising the two lions among men."}}]}]}